last 7 days and last 4 weeks (stars earned & missions attempted), implemented as accessible SVG/CSS bars (no chart library).\n   - FR-DASH-07 Bibi chat history grouped by mission, with a simple topic summary (e.g. count of questions per mission + which hint levels were reached; flagged messages marked).\n   - FR-DASH-08 settings (parent only, or teacher for class students where sensible): daily learning limit in minutes (null = no limit; options e.g. 15/30/45/60/none), reset PIN (shows new PIN once), toggle sound, delete child data (confirm step), and NFR-SC-04 export all child data as JSON (Route Handler `src/app/api/export/anak/[id]/route.ts` with the same access check, `Content-Disposition: attachment`).\n5. `/dashboard/kelas/[id]` — teacher class view (only the owning teacher): shows class code + invite instructions (students open `/masuk`, choose \"Kode Kelas\", enter the code, then pick their name + PIN, or join as new student) (FR-DASH-06). FR-DASH-05: student table sortable (name, stars, score, last active) and filterable (search + filter \"Perlu bantuan\" / \"Tidak aktif\"), with flags: inactive = no attempt in last 7 days (or never), struggling = many failed attempts (e.g. ≥ 6 fails and fail ratio > 0.75 in last 14 days). Teacher can add a student (nickname, avatar, grade → shows generated PIN once). Each row links to `/dashboard/anak/[id]`. FR-DASH-09 export class CSV via route handler `src/app/api/export/kelas/[id]/route.ts`.\n\n## Existing code you MUST reuse (read these files first; do not modify them unless there's a real bug — tell me if so)\n- `prisma/schema.prisma` — models User(role \"PARENT\"|\"TEACHER\", familyCode), Class(code), ChildProfile(nickname, avatar, grade, pinHash, parentId, classId, consentAt, dailyLimitMin, soundOn, lastActiveAt), Progress, Attempt, ChildBadge, ChatLog.\n- `src/lib/db.ts` (`db` Prisma client), `src/lib/session.ts` (`createAdultSession`, `getAdultSession`, `requireAdult`, `clearAdultSession`, `adultCanAccessChild`), `src/lib/codes.ts` (`randomCode`, `randomPin`, `normalizeCode`), `src/lib/constants.ts` (`AVATARS`, `GRADES`).\n- `src/lib/missions/gamification.ts` — `totals(progress)`, `rankFor`, `conceptMastery(concept, progress, attempts)`, `BADGES`, `badgeById`, `starsInLevel`, `maxStarsInLevel`. `src/content/missions.ts` — `MISSIONS`, `LEVELS`, `missionsByLevel`, `getMission`.\n- Design tokens/utilities in `src/app/globals.css` (Tailwind v4): colors `peach`, `navy`, `orange`, `orange-700` (orange text), `cta`, `leaf`, `leaf-700`, `sky`, `berry`, `sun`, `ink`; utilities `btn-primary`, `btn-navy`, `btn-ghost`, `btn-leaf`, `card`, `chip`, `input`, `label`; fonts `font-display`/`font-sans`. `@/components/brand/Logo`, `@/components/brand/BibiMascot`.\n- Next.js 16 notes: `params` and `searchParams` are Promises (`const { id } = await params`), `cookies()` is async. Don't use middleware/proxy; protect each page server-side.\n\n## Requirements\n- Dashboard must be visually separated from the kids area (NFR-UX-07): put a shared layout at `src/app/dashboard/layout.tsx` with a calmer adult header (Logo, user name, role badge, logout). Put auth pages under `src/app/akun/`.\n- RBAC everywhere (NFR-SC-03): every server action re-checks session + ownership. Never trust IDs from the client.\n- Responsive, accessible (labels, ARIA, keyboard), WCAG AA contrast.\n- Put reusable dashboard components in `src/components/dashboard/` and server actions in `src/app/akun/actions.ts` and `src/app/dashboard/actions.ts`. Data-loading helpers may go in `src/lib/dashboard.ts`.\n- Do NOT create/edit files outside: `src/app/akun/**`, `src/app/dashboard/**`, `src/app/api/export/**`, `src/components/dashboard/**`, `src/lib/dashboard.ts`. Other agents are concurrently building `/` (landing), `/masuk`, `/peta`, `/misi` and `/api/bibi`, `/api/progress`.\n\n## Environment notes\n- Windows + PowerShell. `npm`/`npx` are blocked by execution policy: use `npm.cmd` / `npx.cmd`. Filesystem is slow; commands may take minutes.\n- Do NOT run `npm install`, `next dev`, `next build`, or Prisma migrations (I will run them). Dependencies may still be installing; once `node_modules/typescript` and `node_modules/.prisma/client` exist you may run `npx.cmd tsc --noEmit -p e:\\codekids` and only fix errors in your own files. If `@prisma/client` types are not generated yet, you may run `npx.cmd prisma generate` once.\n\nWhen done, reply with a concise summary of routes/files created and anything I need to know.","Role":"Dashboard & Auth Builder","TypeName":"self"}],"toolAction":"Relaunching subagents","toolSummary":"Relaunch subagents"}}]}
